{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788198065,"nonce":"j1tmr5lGHOd2wha6n+v74jkwrCA=","message":"CLOSED — audited, fixed, merged and verified in-game on BORGES.\nMerged `99a54e3`; audit fix `d31ed19`; DLL `09a4ace`.\n**The eight previously-unreachable 3.4 checks now pass.**\n\n\n`RimWorld/MainTabWindow_Work.DoManualPrioritiesCheckbox` confirmed verbatim: it\nwrites `Current.Game.playSettings.useWorkPriorities` and then, `if` it changed,\nfans `Notify_UseWorkPrioritiesChanged()` to every `PawnsFinder\n.AllMapsWorldAndTemporary_Alive` pawn in the player faction with `workSettings`.\n\n`Pawn_WorkSettings.Notify_UseWorkPrioritiesChanged` is `workGiversDirty = true`,\nand `WorkGiversInOrderNormal/Emergency` call `CacheWorkGiversInOrder()` only when\nthat flag is set. **Grepping the member over the whole 1.6 tree returns exactly\nTWO hits — the declaration and that one call site.** So nothing else in the game\ndirties the cache for this reason, and a bare field write really is inert. The\n\"a widget's citation-worthy content can be its EFFECT, not its gate\" finding is\nconfirmed at the strongest available level.\n\nAlso verified: default OFF (`Scribe_Values.Look(..., defaultValue: false)`, no\ninitialiser); the flip is lossless because `GetPriority` masks at READ time; a\nwrite while OFF flattens to 0/3 (`WidgetsWork.DrawWorkBoxFor` and\n`PawnColumnWorker_WorkPriority.HeaderClicked` both write only 0 and 3);\n`PawnsFinder`'s statics are Clear/AddRange/return with no lazy init and no `Rand`.\n\n**Lever ORDER is correct** — checked deliberately for the `39c9db7` warden shape,\nwhere a mode gate was evaluated before the lever feeding it was applied. Here the\nflip lands before the refusal loop reads `usePriorities`.\n\n\n`work-priorities`' matrix path **never calls `outcome.Ok`** — its unit is cells,\nso it fills `changes` and overwrites `result[\"accepted\"]` AFTER\n`Outcome.Result` has already computed `[\"action\"] = Accepted.Count \u003e 0 ?\nStamp(seq) : NoStamp()`. Every successful matrix write therefore returned\n`action {journal_seq: null, provenance: \"not applicable — nothing was mutated\"}`\nover a call that had just journaled.\n\nPre-existing on `main` and **invisible until this branch made 4.7 reachable** —\nand 3.4's check `4.7e` asserts `data.action.journal_seq \u003e= 1`. So without the fix\nthis branch would have failed one of the very eight checks it exists to deliver.\nIndependently re-verified by the orchestrator at `PawnActs.cs` `Outcome.Result`\nbefore merge.\n\n\n     1  pawn {sections:[\"work\"]}        -\u003e use_priorities: FALSE   (the bug)\n     2  work-priorities {manual:true}   -\u003e before:false after:true changed:true\n                                          pawns_notified: 8   journal_seq: 15\n     3  pawn {sections:[\"work\"]}        -\u003e use_priorities: true  (observer agrees)\n     4  work-priorities {set:[Doctor=1]}-\u003e cells:1 after:1\n                                          action.journal_seq: 16   \u003c- THE FIX\n                                          (null before d31ed19)\n     5  pawn -\u003e Doctor priority 1\n     6  work-priorities {manual:false}  -\u003e changed:true notified:8\n     7  pawn -\u003e Doctor reads 3          (GetPriority's read-time mask)\n     8  work-priorities {set:[Doctor=1]}-\u003e ok:FALSE bad-args, refusal preserved\n     9  work-priorities {manual:true}\n    10  pawn -\u003e Doctor reads 1 AGAIN    \u003c- LOSSLESS across the off/on cycle\n    11  work-priorities {manual:true}   -\u003e changed:false notified:0\n                                          journal_seq:null, \"nothing was mutated\"\n                                          (correct here — nothing WAS mutated)\n    13  work-priorities {manual:true, set:[Doctor=2]}\n                                        -\u003e ok:TRUE, mode:matrix, before:1 after:2\n    14  journal action rows: exactly 5 `manual-priorities`, each carrying\n        before/after/pawns_notified, no `cheat` key\n    15  red errors: 0\n\n`pawns_notified: 8` is the load-bearing number — `changed:true` with\n`pawns_notified:0` on a peopled colony would mean the flip is inert, which is the\nwhole defect. Step 10 is the only step that could have falsified losslessness.\nStep 13 is the lever-order proof: the identical call refused at step 8 succeeds\nwhen `manual:true` rides along.\n\n\n`pwsh accept\\3.4-pawn-orders.ps1 -Phase 4,5` on the merged DLL:\n**RESULT: all 82 checks passed.**\n\n- `0.5` reports `manual priorities: False -\u003e True (8 pawn work rows notified)`\n- `4.7a`-`4.7e` PASS (5), with `4.7e` the one `d31ed19` fixes\n- `5.1a`-`5.1c` PASS (3) — priority 2 across a 2x2 cross product\n- `4.12` and `5.18a` — zero red errors; `5.18b` — no modal left behind\n\n\nThe flip runs BEFORE `OnePawn`/`PawnList`/`WorkTypeList`/the priority-range\ncheck, all of which throw. So `{manual:true, set:[{work:\"Docter\", …}]}` returns\n`ok:false` **with the lever already flipped, fanned out and journaled.** That\nordering is what makes the one-call form work, so it is the design; the cost was\nmerely undocumented. Now stated at the flip site and given acceptance step 16.\nMaking it atomic means resolving every `set` block before the flip and\nre-checking the refusal after — a restructure of the matrix loop. **Not done, and\nnot filed as a separate issue: it is a documented cost, not a defect.** Say so if\nyou disagree and it becomes one.\n\n\n- **Behavioural re-prioritisation.** `pawns_notified: 8` is the MECHANICAL claim.\n  No run advanced the clock and watched colonists actually pick different jobs\n  because of the flip. That is the real-world claim and it is unproven.\n- **D2's acceptance step 16** was never executed — the cost is confirmed by\n  reading the code, not by a run.\n- **The caravan gap**, where vanilla's own fan-out omits\n  `AllCaravansAndTravellingTransporters_Alive` and a caravanning colonist keeps a\n  stale WorkGiver order. Reproduced deliberately; not tested.\n- **A roster containing a pawn with `workSettings == null`** — the guard is read,\n  never exercised, so \"zero red errors in the fan-out\" is proved only for this\n  8-pawn colony.\n- **`rwa`'s `--manual` coercion**, read but not run (BORGES has no python).\n- There is still **no `.ps1` driver** for `accept/manual-work-priorities.md`;\n  steps 1-16 above were hand-driven as raw file protocol.","files":null}]}